    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `checkDigit` = a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of `customerCode`, exposed on the owner response. I implemented it following this project's existing pattern for derived response fields (like `locality`, `membershipLevel`, `contactPreference`), which are computed getters on the `Owner` model that MapStruct maps into the generated `OwnerDto`:\n\n1. **`Owner.getCheckDigit()`** (`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`) \u2014 a computed getter that runs the Luhn algorithm over the digits in `customerCode` (ignoring non-digit characters like the `CITY3-LAST3-` separators), returning the single check digit `(10 - sum % 10) % 10`, or `0` when no customer code is assigned. The algorithm matches the test's reference `luhn(...)` exactly.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` integer field (0\u20139) to the owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it from the new getter.\n\nNo new OfficeFloor function was needed since `checkDigit` is a pure derivation of already-assigned state, exposed at the response edge like the other computed fields \u2014 consistent with AGENTS.md's \"keep DTOs at the edges\" guidance.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` (1 test, 0 failures).",
